<article class="env-lemma" id="02GM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02GM">Lemma <span data-tag="02GM">29.37.8</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. If $f$ is flat, locally of finite presentation, and for every $s \in S$ the fibre $X_ s$ is a disjoint union of spectra of finite separable field extensions of $\kappa (s)$, then $f$ is étale. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      You can deduce this from Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00U6" data-tag="00U6">10.143.7</a>. Here is another proof. 
    <p>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/02GL" data-tag="02GL">29.37.7</a> a fibre $X_ s$ is étale and hence smooth over $s$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/01V8" data-tag="01V8">29.35.3</a> we see that $X \to S$ is smooth. By Lemma <a href="/tag/02G8" data-tag="02G8">29.36.12</a> we see that $f$ is unramified. We conclude by Lemma <a href="/tag/02GK" data-tag="02GK">29.37.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>